  "Area": "Unclassified",
  "Number": 5,
  "Question": "A rectangular box has integer side lengths in the ratio \\(1:3:4.\\) Which of the following could be the volume of the box?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(48\\)",
    "B": "\\(56\\)",
    "C": "\\(64\\)",
    "D": "\\(96\\)",
    "E": "\\(144\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Let \\(k\\) be the shortest side length. The ratio \\(1:3:4\\) makes the three dimensions \\(k,3k,4k\\). Since the side lengths are integers, \\(k\\) must be a positive integer. The volume is therefore\n\\[\nV=k\\cdot3k\\cdot4k=12k^3.\n\\]\nFor \\(k=1\\), the volume is \\(12\\), which is not listed. For \\(k=2\\), it is \\(12\\cdot8=96\\). For every \\(k\\ge3\\), it is at least \\(12\\cdot27=324\\), larger than every choice.\n\nThus the only possible listed volume is \\(\\boxed{96}\\), realized by side lengths \\(2,6,8\\). The answer is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
